 going negative</strong> or depositors losing money: While mAPOLLO is intended to be an ‚Äúup-only‚Äù token in terms of exchange rate (similar to other Midas-issued tokens such as mEDGE and mMEV), several risks could still affect performance:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Underlying Strategy Risk: The reference portfolio comprises market-neutral, stablecoin-focused DeFi strategies. Unexpected market events, protocol failures, liquidity shortfalls, or mispricing could lead to reduced returns or losses in the underlying strategies.</li>\n<li>Protocol Risk: Smart contract vulnerabilities, oracle failures, or integration issues with DeFi protocols used in the reference strategies could negatively affect performance.</li>\n<li>Counterparty Risk: The appointed risk manager, Apollo Crypto, and any underlying protocol counterparties could fail to deliver expected execution or risk controls.</li>\n<li>Regulatory/Legal Risk: Changes in applicable laws or enforcement actions could restrict certain strategies or limit product operations.</li>\n<li>Operational Risk: Failures in execution, custody, or settlement infrastructure could cause delays or losses.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Although the token's exchange rate is designed to move upward as yield accrues in the reference portfolio, adverse events in any of the above categories could reduce or eliminate returns.</p>\n<p><strong>From underlying protocol</strong></p>","importantQuirks":"<ul>\n<li>Minor rewards from points will be directly reflected in price updates</li>\n<li>Major rewards are converted into USDC and distributed through Merkl</li>\n<li>Points earned from this pool change dynamically due to the nature of the underlying asset, refer <a href=\"https://midas.app/mapollo\">here</a> for the most updated list of points.</li>\n</ul>\n","initiatedBy":"Midas Team","conversionRate":{"rate":1.120414,"fromUnit":"mAPOLLO","toUnit":"USD worth of USDC staked in Midas' mAPOLLO vault"},"utilizedProtocols":[{"id":"midas","url":"https://midas.app/","name